  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Irregular past",
   "texto": [
    "Many frequent verbs change shape in the past and do not follow regular endings: **å være → var**, **å gå → gikk**, **å dra → dro**. The form is the same with all people: **jeg dro**, **vi dro**.",
    "To ask for a finished fact, the past is also used: **Hvor var du?**, **Hva gjorde dere?**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Other common verbs",
   "texto": [
    "Learn each couple as a unit: **se → så**, **ta → tok**, **ha → hadde**, **få → fikk**. The Norwegian past is usually translated into Spanish with preterite: «I was», «vi», «tomé», «I had», «recibí»."
   ]
  },
